CURRENT PROBLEMS TO SOLVE

1. INFRASTRUCTURE
- Determine exactly where the frontend is hosted.
- Determine where the backend/API is hosted.
- Determine whether Cloudflare Workers/Pages are being used and for what.
- Determine whether an Azure VM is actually required.
- Avoid using an Azure Windows VM only for MongoDB.
- Prefer a low-cost/free architecture where practical.
- Evaluate MongoDB Atlas M0 for development/MVP and determine whether its 512 MB limit is sufficient for current structured data.
- Do NOT store property images/videos/documents directly in MongoDB.
- Verify Cloudflare DNS, HTTPS, API routing, environment variables and deployment.
- Identify any unnecessary Azure resources that can be removed to reduce cost.

